<span class="label">9.</span><cite>Pierce KL, Premont RT, Lefkowitz RJ. Seven-transmembrane receptors. Nat Rev Mol Cell Biol. 2002;3(9):639–650. doi: 10.1038/nrm908.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/nrm908" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12209124/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Nat%20Rev%20Mol%20Cell%20Biol&amp;title=Seven-transmembrane%20receptors&amp;author=KL%20Pierce&amp;author=RT%20Premont&amp;author=RJ%20Lefkowitz&amp;volume=3&amp;issue=9&amp;publication_year=2002&amp;pages=639-650&amp;pmid=12209124&amp;doi=10.1038/nrm908&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
<li id="r10">
<span class="label">10.</span><cite>Reiter E, Lefkowitz RJ. GRKs and beta-arrestins: Roles in receptor silencing, trafficking and signaling. Trends Endocrinol Metab. 2006;17(4):159–165. doi: 10.1016/j.tem.2006.03.008.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tem.2006.03.008" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16595179/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Trends%20Endocrinol%20Metab&amp;title=GRKs%20and%20beta-arrestins:%20Roles%20in%20receptor%20silencing,%20trafficking%20and%20signaling&amp;author=E%20Reiter&amp;author=RJ%20Lefkowitz&amp;volume=17&amp;issue=4&amp;publication_year=2006&amp;pages=159-165&amp;pmid=16595179&amp;doi=10.1016/j.tem.2006.03.008&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
<li id="r11">
